/* book Worked example: Q: A single-phase dual converter feeds a 5 Ω resistance in series with a large inductance from 230 V, 50 Hz. Converter P is fired at α1 = 30°. Find V1 and the load current, and the angle α2 for converter N so that it is ready with the same voltage.
   1. 2Vm/π = 2 × 325.27/π = 207.07 V.
   2. The large inductance keeps the current continuous, so V1 = 207.07 × cos 30° = 179.33 V.
   3. I = V1/R = 179.33/5 = 35.87 A.
   4. α2 = 180° − 30° = 150°. Converter N on its own gives 207.07 × cos 150° = −179.33 V, which, being connected the other way round, is +179.33 V at the load: the two agree.
   Answer: V1 = 179.3 V, I = 35.9 A, α2 = 150°. */
